Cycle compression is a reliable indicator of system failure. When the intervals between crises approach zero, the buffer that allows each party to recover and re-engage is gone. Both parties are now operating in a state of uninterrupted crisis. There is no longer a baseline to return to. The 'good periods' that Dan refers to repeatedly in the early record — the moments that sustained his hope — have effectively ceased to exist.

